      "content": "\"Monet's 'Water Lilies' series, created between 1897 and 1926, consists of approximately 250 oil paintings. The collection represents Monet's fascination with the interplay of light and water on the banks of his garden at Giverny. The dimensions of the paintings vary, with some pieces measuring up to 6 feet in height and 8 feet in width. The pigments used by Monet in this series include oil paints, with a palette that predominantly features earth tones, blues, and greens. The historical context of the paintings is rooted in the post-Impressionist movement, reflecting Monet's continued exploration of natural light and his departure from the precise representation of reality.\"",
